{"content_hash": "6f6be10bfaf72a83", "version_id": 571, "article_id": 58, "level_code": "en_a1", "lang": "en", "level": 1, "level_label": "A1 入门", "title": "Nikon says top photo prize goes to an AI picture", "title_zh": "尼康说，一张AI图片拿了摄影大奖", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "bbc_tech", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr86z33pdy9vo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1614036417651-efe5912149d8?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8cHJpemUlMjB3aW5uaW5nJTIwaW1hZ2V8ZW58MHwwfHx8MTc5MTc2NTYxNXww&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Brands&People on Unsplash", "author": "Brands&People", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@brandsandpeople?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/yellow-paper-award-ribbon-ZdqSuxl3Lak?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(16, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(54, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "cec84960fed8"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-09", "word_count": 81, "reading_minutes": 0.4, "lead": "A science photo contest gave a prize to a video. Then people said the video was not real. Nikon looked at it again.", "lead_zh": "一个科学摄影比赛把奖颁给了一段视频。后来有人说，这段视频不是真的。尼康又重新检查了一遍。", "preview": "Nikon runs a big photo contest for tiny things. The winner was a video from Dr Ning Xu in China.", "preview_zh": "尼康办了一个拍微小东西的摄影大赛。获奖的是中国徐宁博士的一段视频。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 560, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/58/en_a1.mp3", "duration": 33.387, "size_bytes": 204192, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 92, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@86b1023/content/data/versions/571.json", "paragraphs": ["Nikon runs a big photo contest for tiny things. The winner was a video from Dr Ning Xu in China.", "Other scientists said the video was not real. They said AI made it. Nikon looked at the video again.", "Nikon said the video broke the rules. AI is not allowed in this contest. So Nikon took the prize away.", "Dr Robert Hirst is a scientist in the UK. He said he knew at once. He studies sick children for 20 years."], "paragraphs_zh": ["尼康办了一个拍微小东西的摄影大赛。获奖的是中国徐宁博士的一段视频。", "其他科学家说这段视频不是真的。他们说这是AI做的。尼康又看了一遍视频。", "尼康说这段视频违反了规则。这个比赛不许用AI。所以尼康把奖收回了。", "罗伯特·赫斯特博士是英国的一位科学家。他说他一下就知道了。他研究生病的孩子已经20年。"], "body": "Nikon runs a big photo contest for tiny things. The winner was a video from Dr Ning Xu in China.\n\nOther scientists said the video was not real. They said AI made it. Nikon looked at the video again.\n\nNikon said the video broke the rules. AI is not allowed in this contest. So Nikon took the prize away.\n\nDr Robert Hirst is a scientist in the UK. He said he knew at once. He studies sick children for 20 years.", "body_zh": "尼康办了一个拍微小东西的摄影大赛。获奖的是中国徐宁博士的一段视频。\n\n其他科学家说这段视频不是真的。他们说这是AI做的。尼康又看了一遍视频。\n\n尼康说这段视频违反了规则。这个比赛不许用AI。所以尼康把奖收回了。\n\n罗伯特·赫斯特博士是英国的一位科学家。他说他一下就知道了。他研究生病的孩子已经20年。", "text": "Nikon runs a big photo contest for tiny things. The winner was a video from Dr Ning Xu in China. Other scientists said the video was not real. They said AI made it. Nikon looked at the video again. Nikon said the video broke the rules. AI is not allowed in this contest. So Nikon took the prize away. Dr Robert Hirst is a scientist in the UK. He said he knew at once. He studies sick children for 20 years.", "vocab": [{"word": "prize", "pos": "noun", "zh": "奖；奖品", "note": "比赛赢了拿到的东西", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "contest", "pos": "noun", "zh": "比赛", "note": "和 competition 意思相近", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "video", "pos": "noun", "zh": "视频", "note": "可以拍、可以看", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "real", "pos": "adj", "zh": "真的", "note": "反义词是 fake（假的）", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "rule", "pos": "noun", "zh": "规则", "note": "常用复数 rules", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "allow", "pos": "verb", "zh": "允许", "note": "not allowed 就是“不允许”", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "scientist", "pos": "noun", "zh": "科学家", "note": "做科学研究的人", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "study", "pos": "verb", "zh": "研究", "note": "也可以当名词：学习、研究", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Prize-winning image which sparked backlash was AI-generated, Nikon rules", "summary_original": "The camera-maker says it is now re-evaluating the rules and procedures of its Small World in Motion contest.", "body_original": "Prize-winning image which sparked backlash was AI-generated, Nikon rules\nBy\nZoe Kleinman\nTechnology & AI editor\nPublished\n9 October 2026\nThe winner of a prestigious scientific photography competition has been disqualified following concerns raised by other scientists that it was fake.\nNikon said the use of generative AI in the composition of the video broke the rules of its Small World In Motion contest, which accepts photos and video taken using powerful microscopes.\nThe firm said the video \"did not comply with the competition rules regarding generative AI\", but added it was not a judgement of the entrant's professional reputation or scientific contributions.\nIt said it would now look at the rules and procedures of the annual contest, which has been running for 15 years and is specifically for microscopic images.\nNikon said it came to the decision \"after thoroughly re-evaluating the video and supporting materials and consulting with members of our judging panel\".\nThe winning entry came from Dr Ning Xu, from Tsinghua University in China, who submitted a short video showing tiny, hair-like structures called cilia moving in the airway of a child with the respiratory condition PCD.\nThe BBC has approached him for comment.\nA number of scientists, including former competition judges, complained to Nikon on its LinkedIn page that the video did not appear to be real.\nXu had acknowledged using AI, but said he believed he had acted within the rules, and had cooperated with Nikon's investigation.\nUniversity of Leicester scientist Dr Robert Hirst, who was among the first experts to voice concerns, said he was \"not surprised\" and he \"knew immediately that the video was fabricated\".\n\"I have been diagnosing PCD for 20 years by examining their cilia waveform, length, cell size and shape,\" he said.\nHirst, who is lead scientist for the NHS centre for PCD diagnosis at the university, said the cells and cilia \"look nothing like those from PCD patients\".\n\"This controversy has impacted a lot of patients, scientists, doctors and PCD support networks around the world,\" he said.\nTiny image sparks big backlash in Nikon photo contest\nPublished\n1 October\nWhat is AI, how does it work and why are some people concerned about it?\nPublished\n14 September\nSign up for our Tech Decoded newsletter\nto follow the world's top tech stories and trends.\nOutside the UK? Sign up here\n.\nRelated topics\nArtificial intelligence\nPhotography\nScience & Environment", "fetched_at": "2026-10-12T00:40:13.616651", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Nikon", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.675, "sm": 100, "em": 674, "cs": 0, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "runs", "s": 0.688, "e": 0.925, "sm": 687, "em": 925, "cs": 6, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "a", "s": 0.938, "e": 1.012, "sm": 937, "em": 1012, "cs": 11, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "big", "s": 1.025, "e": 1.25, "sm": 1025, "em": 1250, "cs": 13, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "photo", "s": 1.262, "e": 1.575, "sm": 1262, "em": 1575, "cs": 17, "ce": 22, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "contest", "s": 1.587, "e": 2.175, "sm": 1587, "em": 2175, "cs": 23, "ce": 30, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "for", "s": 2.188, "e": 2.3, "sm": 2187, "em": 2300, "cs": 31, "ce": 34, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "tiny", "s": 2.312, "e": 2.625, "sm": 2312, "em": 2625, "cs": 35, "ce": 39, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "things", "s": 2.638, "e": 3.213, "sm": 2637, "em": 3212, "cs": 4